from pathlib import Path
import json,html,shutil
ROOT=Path(__file__).resolve().parent;S=ROOT/'site';rows=json.loads((S/'analysis_summary.json').read_text())
CSS='''*{box-sizing:border-box}body{margin:20px;background:#10151e;color:#e7eef7;font:16px/1.45 system-ui,Arial,sans-serif}a{color:#a4d9ff}h1{font-size:27px}h2{font-size:21px;margin:18px 0 10px}.muted{color:#b7c8dc}.warning{border-left:4px solid #efc37b;background:#292619;padding:12px 16px;max-width:1400px}.tabs{display:flex;gap:8px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin:16px 0}.tabs button{background:#22344c;color:#e9f4ff;border:1px solid #577392;padding:9px 15px;border-radius:6px;cursor:pointer}.tabs button.active{background:#446c92}.grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(235px,1fr));gap:15px;max-width:1500px}figure{margin:0}figure img{width:100%;height:auto;display:block;background:#131923}figcaption{color:#bed0e5;font-size:13px;margin-top:5px}select,input{background:#263950;color:white;border:1px solid #7893b0;padding:9px;font:inherit;border-radius:6px}.controls{display:flex;gap:14px;align-items:center;flex-wrap:wrap;margin:14px 0}.card{padding:10px;background:#1b2839;border:1px solid #354e69;border-radius:9px}.card img{width:100%;height:210px;object-fit:cover}.card h3{font-size:17px;margin:4px 0}table{border-collapse:collapse}th,td{padding:8px;border:1px solid #4c607a;text-align:left}section[hidden]{display:none}p{max-width:1200px}'''
methods={'track_v2':'Track-V2','gabor_curved':'Curved Gabor','fourier':'Fourier','sparcfire':'SpArcFiRe'}

def figure(stem,title,name,cl=''):
 return f'<figure><img class="{cl}" loading="lazy" src="images/{stem}/{name}" alt="{html.escape(title)}"><figcaption>{html.escape(title)}</figcaption></figure>'
for row in rows:
 stem=row['stem'];q=html.escape(stem);ok=row['status']=='ok';warn=[]
 if row.get('quality_flags'):warn+=row['quality_flags']
 if row.get('warning'):warn.append(row['warning'])
 msg='; '.join(warn) or 'Uncalibrated or mixed-survey imaging; all measurements exploratory.'
 text=f'<!doctype html><html><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>{q} | NearbySpiralsTEST</title><style>{CSS}</style></head><body><a href="index.html">← All 35 nearby galaxies</a><h1>{q}</h1><div class="warning">Research TEST — not validated physical arm pitches or a calibrated GALFIT decomposition. {html.escape(msg)}</div>'
 if ok:
  opts=''.join(f'<option value="{m}">{name}</option>' for m,name in methods.items())
  text+='<nav class="tabs"><button class="active" data-tab="pitches" onclick="tab(\'pitches\')">Face-on & pitches</button><button data-tab="model" onclick="tab(\'model\')">Bulge / disk / bar / arms</button><button data-tab="qc" onclick="tab(\'qc\')">Quality & provenance</button></nav>'
  text+=f'<div class="controls"><label>Method <select id="method" onchange="method(this.value)">{opts}</select></label></div>'
  text+='<section id="pitches"><h2>Original and deprojected arm geometry</h2><div class="grid">'+figure(stem,'Original color reference','original.jpg')+figure(stem,'Native g-band image','native_g.png')+figure(stem,'Candidate arm curves over original','track_v2_overlay.jpg','method-overlay')+figure(stem,'Candidate arm curves in face-on frame','track_v2_face.jpg','method-face')+'</div><h2>Detection evidence</h2><div class="grid">'+figure(stem,'Curved Gabor ridge response (not physical brightness)','gabor_response.png')+figure(stem,'Deprojected component-subtraction residual','face_residual.png')+'</div></section>'
  text+='<section id="model" hidden><h2>Provisional smooth components</h2><p class="muted">Disk and bulge are an exploratory two-component fit to radial medians, not a validated PSF-convolved GALFIT model. Bar is explicitly not fitted and is displayed as zero.</p><div class="grid">'+figure(stem,'Bulge — provisional','bulge.png')+figure(stem,'Disk — provisional','disk.png')+figure(stem,'Bar — not fitted (zero)','bar.png')+figure(stem,'Bulge + disk + bar (bar=0)','smooth.png')+'</div><h2>Arm-light reconstruction</h2><div class="grid">'+figure(stem,'Original image','original.jpg')+figure(stem,'Arms only','track_v2_arms.png','method-arms')+figure(stem,'Smooth + fitted arms','track_v2_model.png','method-model')+figure(stem,'Residual after subtracting model','track_v2_residual.png','method-residual')+'</div><h2>Signed residuals</h2><div class="grid">'+figure(stem,'Before arms: original − sky − (bulge + disk)','before.png')+figure(stem,'After arms: before − fitted arms','track_v2_residual.png','method-residual')+'</div><p class="muted">Red: positive residual. Blue: excess model. Both are signed differences in FITS pixel units, using the same residual display scale. Light fitting is in-sample and may overfit.</p></section>'
  text+='<section id="qc" hidden><h2>Method-by-method diagnostic summary</h2><table><tr><th>Method</th><th>Candidate curves</th><th>Pitch labels</th><th>In-sample SSE reduction</th></tr>'
  for m,name in methods.items():
   r=row['methods'][m];pitch=', '.join(f'{p:.1f}°' for p in r['pitches_deg']) or 'No reliable curve'
   text+=f'<tr><td>{name}</td><td>{r["segments"]}</td><td>{pitch}</td><td>{r["residual_sse_reduction_fraction"]*100:.1f}%</td></tr>'
  text+='</table><p>Track-V2 and Fourier are carried forward from the earlier nearby-galaxy exploratory analysis. Curved Gabor ridge candidates and provisional brightness fits are newly calculated from the supplied FITS frames. SpArcFiRe uses the installed r140 engine in single-turn mode on the saved AutoProf deprojection; no full radial peak-graph rerun is claimed here.</p>'
  text+=f'<p><a href="images/{stem}/result.json">Full per-galaxy JSON</a> | <a href="README.md">Method limitations</a></p></section>'
  text+=f'''<script>const stem={json.dumps(stem)};function tab(k){{for(const s of ['pitches','model','qc'])document.getElementById(s).hidden=s!==k;document.querySelectorAll('[data-tab]').forEach(b=>b.classList.toggle('active',b.dataset.tab===k));}}function method(k){{for(const cls of ['overlay','face','arms','model','residual'])document.querySelectorAll('.method-'+cls).forEach(im=>im.src='images/'+stem+'/'+k+'_'+cls+(cls==='overlay'||cls==='face'?'.jpg':'.png'));}}</script>'''
 else:text+='<h2>Analysis unavailable</h2><p>AutoProf geometry or usable component inputs are missing. The original FITS frame is preserved without fabricated pitch measurements.</p>'+figure(stem,'Original color or grayscale reference','original.jpg')
 text+='</body></html>'
 (S/(stem+'.html')).write_text(text,encoding='utf-8')
# Overview: all 35, including flagged or failed objects.
counts={m:sum(r.get('methods',{}).get(m,{}).get('segments',0)>0 for r in rows) for m in methods}
items=''
for r in rows:
 s=r['stem'];flag=r['status'];pitches=r.get('methods',{}).get('track_v2',{}).get('pitches_deg',[])
 items+=f'<article class="card" data-name="{s.lower()}"><a href="{s}.html"><h3>{s}</h3><img loading="lazy" src="images/{s}/original.jpg"></a><p class="muted">{html.escape(flag)} | Track-V2: {len(pitches)} curves</p></article>'
index=f'<!doctype html><html><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>NearbySpiralsTEST | 35 galaxies</title><style>{CSS}</style></head><body><h1>NearbySpiralsTEST</h1><p>35 nearby galaxies — exploratory spiral-arm overlays and model reconstructions.</p><div class="warning"><b>Scientific caution:</b> these images come from mixed survey sources, some without calibrated photometry or reliable inclination. This test gallery does not establish physical pitch angles or trustworthy bulge-to-total ratios. The smooth model is a provisional radial-profile approximation, not a GALFIT decomposition. Inspect the per-galaxy quality tab before interpreting any result.</div><p>Candidate curves present: '+', '.join(f'{name}: {counts[m]}/35' for m,name in methods.items())+'.</p><p><a href="README.md">Methods, limitations, and provenance</a> | <a href="analysis_summary.json">All result metadata</a></p><div class="controls"><input placeholder="Find a galaxy" oninput="document.querySelectorAll(\'.card\').forEach(x=>x.hidden=!x.dataset.name.includes(this.value.toLowerCase()))"></div><div class="grid">{items}</div></body></html>'
(S/'index.html').write_text(index,encoding='utf-8');(S/'.nojekyll').write_text('')
(S/'README.md').write_text('''# NearbySpiralsTEST\n\nAn exploratory, clearly quality-flagged presentation of the 35 galaxies in `Nearby_IMBH/JUST_THE_35_GALAXIES`. No source FITS or prior scientific result was overwritten.\n\n## Inputs\n\n35 512×512 FITS frames, 34 existing color references, saved AutoProf geometry where available, saved Gaia foreground-star masks where available, and saved exploratory Track-V2 and Fourier candidate overlays from BIRTHDAY_GITHUB_STYLE_V6. The sample combines DSS2 and Legacy survey images; flux units, PSFs and calibration are not uniform.\n\n## Methods\n\n- Track-V2: earlier candidate log-spiral traces reused as saved. No new Track-V2 detection run is claimed.\n- Curved Gabor: structure-tensor direction field and local curved sampling to enhance ridges in the provisional smooth-subtracted image. Skeleton-connected fragments propose tracks; these are **not** validated physical arms, and disconnected branches can be misinterpreted.\n- Fourier: saved exploratory Fourier components reused as saved. No multi-peak/multi-mode reanalysis is claimed.\n- SpArcFiRe: genuine installed compiled r140 engine, single-turn configuration, run on AutoProf-deprojected image frames. Arcs are screened for valid pitch and extent. The engine may detect stellar clumps or spurious structure; these are exploratory, not confirmed arms.\n- Bulge and disk: a new robust two-component **radial-median approximation**, exponential disk and fixed-index n=2 bulge-like profile, not GALFIT, not PSF-convolved, not a calibrated mass decomposition. Bar was **not fitted** and its panel is zero. No B/T should be inferred.\n- Arm light: one nonnegative 2.5-native-pixel Gaussian ribbon per candidate path fitted to the original component-subtracted pixel values. This is in-sample and can overfit. No physical interpretation is assigned to amplitudes.\n\n## Residual arithmetic\n\n`before = (observed - estimated sky) - (provisional bulge + provisional disk + zero bar)`; `after = before - fitted arm light`. Both are signed numerical differences in FITS image units before visualization.\n\n## Known limitations\n\nMany AutoProf inclination estimates are unstable, foreground stars and star-forming clumps can be mistaken for arms, and original images are not uniformly calibrated. UGCA105 has no reliable AutoProf geometry in the saved analysis. High-inclination objects are unsuitable for precise pitch. M33, NGC300 and NGC7793 have published central black-hole constraints and should not be presented as unconstrained new IMBH candidates. This site is a method test, not a validated black-hole candidate catalog.\n\nThe source scripts are preserved separately on the authorized local computer at `E:/Astro/NearbySpiralsTEST_Work`. Raw FITS, original working catalogs, and personal filesystem contents are not published.\n''',encoding='utf-8')
print('SITE_READY',len(rows),counts)
